  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>For a reversible&nbsp;reaction, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8652;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>,&nbsp;which one of the following statement is wrong from the given energy&nbsp;profile diagram?</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/49261fae-32be-464e-9203-417a7208ee0d-image.png\" style=\"width: 593px; height: 397px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "lu4z4",
      "text": "Activation energy of forward reaction is greater than backward reaction",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "OiGAn",
      "text": "The forward reaction is endothermic",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "rPbxM",
      "text": "The threshold energy is less than that of activation energy",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5u33b",
      "text": "The energy of activation of forward reaction is equal to the sum of heat of reaction and the energy of activation of backward reaction",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/49261fae-32be-464e-9203-417a7208ee0d-image.png\" style=\"width: 593px; height: 397px;\" /></p><p>where, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo></math> activation energy of forward reaction</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo></math> activation energy of backward reaction</p><p>The above energy profile diagram shows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></math></p><p>The potential energy of the product is greater than that of the reactant, so the reaction is endothermic.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>&#916;E</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
